    "title": "O'Connell hopes McCarthy builds off first game - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Grant Sweeter No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nEAGAN, MN (KELO) — The Minnesota Vikings scored 21 fourth quarter points on Monday night, to come from behind and beat the Bears 27-24.\nMinnesota is looking to build off a win, where J.J. McCarthy found his footing late, throwing for 143 yards and totaling three scores.\nThat performance helped McCarthy to be named NFC Offensive Player of the Week, but coach Kevin O’Connell wants the young QB to build off the performance.\n“It starts today and it starts with his preparation again. I thought he had a great week of preparation that led him into being able to overcome some adversity and help lead us out of a place where we went playing very well offensively. We found a way to get on track,” O’Connell said.\nThe Vikings are set to host Atlanta on Sunday night at 7:20 p.m.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KELOLAND.com.",
